5TH PROGRAM – Docker + GitHub + Jenkins Setup
================================================

STEP 1: Create Project Folder
-----------------------------
mkdir my-python-app
cd my-python-app

STEP 2: Create Required Files
-----------------------------
nano app.py
nano Dockerfile
nano requirements.txt

STEP 3: Initialize Git Repository
---------------------------------
git init

STEP 4: Configure Git Username and Email
----------------------------------------
git config --global user.name "your_username"
git config --global user.email "your_email@gmail.com"

Example:
git config --global user.name "akshay"
git config --global user.email "akshay@gmail.com"

STEP 5: Add and Commit Files
----------------------------
git add .
git commit -m "initial commit"

STEP 6: Install Java (for Jenkins)
----------------------------------
sudo apt install openjdk-21-jdk

Check Java version:
java -version

STEP 7: Push Code to GitHub
---------------------------
Create a repository in GitHub named:
my-python-app

Push commands:
git remote add origin https://github.com/your-username/my-python-app.git
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main

STEP 8: Build Docker Image
--------------------------
sudo docker build -t my-python-app .

Tag the image:
docker tag my-python-app:latest your-dockerhub-username/my-python-app:latest

Check Docker images:
docker images

STEP 9: Run Docker Container
----------------------------
sudo docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --name mypython-app-container your-dockerhub-username/my-python-app:latest

Check running containers:
docker ps

Login to DockerHub:
docker login -u your-dockerhub-username

Push image to DockerHub:
sudo docker push your-dockerhub-username/my-python-app:latest

STEP 10: Install Jenkins
------------------------
sudo apt update

Add Jenkins repository key:
wget -q -O - https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable/jenkins.io.key | sudo apt-key add -

Add Jenkins repository:
sudo sh -c 'echo deb https://pkg.jenkins.io/debian-stable binary/ > /etc/apt/sources.list.d/jenkins.list'

Install Jenkins:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install jenkins -y

STEP 11: Start Jenkins
----------------------
sudo systemctl start jenkins
sudo systemctl enable jenkins

STEP 12: Open Jenkins
---------------------
Open browser and use:
http://localhost:8080

Useful Commands
---------------
Check Docker containers:
docker ps

Check Docker images:
docker images

Check Jenkins status:
sudo systemctl status jenkins
